CORE
fold_forms.cpp
--cpp17
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ unary right: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ unary left: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.3\] line \d+ binary right: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.4\] line \d+ lockstep: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.5\] line \d+ trait: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.6\] line \d+ empty pack: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.7\] line \d+ class scope: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.8\] line \d+ WRONG \(must FAIL\): FAILURE$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
^CONVERSION ERROR$
--
N5008 [expr.prim.fold]/1-3, [temp.variadic]/5: unary and binary folds whose
pattern names the template's TYPE pack (`sizeof(Ts)', `same<Ts,
int>::value'), alone or together with the function parameter pack
(expanded in lockstep), over an empty pack, and in a class template's
static member initializer.  On bin53 the binary `(init || ... || E)' form
did not parse (only `|' had a binary form; `&&' and `||' had only the
unary one), and a type-pack-only pattern was not expanded.  g++ 13 and
clang++ 18 accept the program.
